<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malayan Communist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Communist Party of Malaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malayan Communist Party was a communist party founded in 1930, drawing its support mainly from the Chinese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>. It led the main resistance to the Japanese occupation and, under Chin Peng, launched an armed revolt in 1948 that the British fought as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malayan-emergency">Malayan Emergency</a> until 1960. Its remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a> fought a second insurgency along the Thai border until a peace agreement signed at Hat Yai in December 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malayan-communist-party.jpg" alt="Malayan Communist Party" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original work by Eureka287, vector work by Lasse Havelund, final edit by ComradeBlots · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Communist_Party_of_Vietnam_flag_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
